    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: level rules \u2192 points system\n\nThe old rule computed `membershipLevel` directly (base 1, +1 per factor, capped at 4). I replaced it with a points system and now return **both** `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel`.\n\n**Points** (start at 0): +2 email present, +1 `namesakeCount == 0`, +2 household of 3+, +3 tenure > 365 days.\n**Level** from points: 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n\n### Files changed\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `membershipPoints` schema field (readOnly, `minimum: 0`) and rewrote `membershipLevel` (now `maximum: 4`, derived-from-points description). The `OwnerDto` getters/setters are generated from this at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `membershipPoints` mapping plus two static helpers, `membershipPointsFor(owner, householdSize)` and `membershipLevelFor(points)`, that hold the arithmetic. The `@Named` mapper methods (`toMembershipPoints`, `toMembershipLevel`) compute using the Owner-derivable factors only.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Household size is a *count* of other owners, which the stateless mapper can't see (same situation as the existing `bulkSignupWarning` flag). So `toOwnerDtoWithBulkWarning` \u2014 the single helper used by the create, get, and list read paths \u2014 counts household members (owners sharing `householdId`, mirroring the existing household-duplicate check) and sets `membershipPoints`/`membershipLevel` with the household bonus applied. The audit log now reports the household-aware level.\n\n### Verification\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsPointsAndLevel` (fresh owner, email + no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure \u2192 3 points, level 2) passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS` (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\nOne note on the household factor: household size isn't stored on the `Owner`, so I derive it by counting owners sharing the same `householdId` at map time \u2014 the same data source and filtering the existing household-duplicate logic uses. The test only exercises the single-member case (bonus not triggered), but the +2 rule is fully wired for real 3+ households.",
