    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of what happens when you create an owner via `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:137-179`).\n\n## Validations (in execution order)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must have the OWNER_ADMIN role (else 403).\n2. **DTO Bean Validation** on `OwnerFieldsDto` (`@Valid @RequestBody`), field by field:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words separated by space/`'`/`-`)\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern` (`^[-0-9 ().+]*$`, permissive)\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, nullable\n   - `postcode` \u2014 nullable, no constraint here\n   - Failures \u2192 **400**.\n3. **Required-field checks** \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (checked after normalization), `city`, `telephone` must be non-blank; missing ones collected \u2192 `MissingRequiredFieldsException` (**400**).\n4. **Postcode validation** \u2014 if present, must match `^[0-9]{4}$`; and if the city maps to a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), the 4 digits must fall in that region's range \u2192 else `InvalidFieldValueException` (**400**).\n5. **Registration-date validation** \u2014 if supplied, must not be in the future \u2192 else `InvalidFieldValueException` (**400**).\n6. **Daily-limit check** \u2014 after defaulting/business-day roll, rejects if \u2265100 owners already share that registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (**429**).\n7. **City-capacity check** \u2014 rejects if \u226550 owners already in that city (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n8. **Telephone E.164 validation** \u2014 normalization must yield a valid `+`-prefixed number with correct national length \u2192 else `InvalidFieldValueException` (**400**).\n9. **Email validation** \u2014 if present, must match the email pattern and not be a disposable domain (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail) \u2192 else `InvalidFieldValueException` (**400**).\n10. **Unique-identity check** \u2014 computed `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`) must not exactly match any existing owner \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n11. **Household-duplicate check** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold=true` or no postcode, rejects if any existing owner shares the `householdId` \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n12. **Entity-level Bean Validation at flush** \u2014 Hibernate re-validates the managed `Owner`: `@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone and E.164 `@Pattern` on telephone.\n\n## Side-effects (in execution order)\n\n1. **Address normalization** \u2014 `address` normalized before the blank check and stored normalized.\n2. **Registration-date defaulting** \u2014 defaults to `LocalDate.now()` if absent.\n3. **Business-day roll** \u2014 Saturday/Sunday registration dates rolled forward to Monday.\n4. **Telephone normalization** \u2014 converted to E.164 (assumes `+61` if no country code) and written back onto the DTO.\n5. **Email normalization** \u2014 trimmed and lower-cased, written back onto the DTO.\n6. **`customerCode` generated** \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, hash of normalized telephone + last name.\n7. **`namesakeCount` set** \u2014 count of existing owners with the same first+last name.\n8. **`householdId` set** \u2014 hash of last name + postcode (null when no postcode).\n9. **Possible-duplicate marking** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` if an earlier owner in the same household has a different phone (unless opted out).\n10. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` inside a `@Transactional` (JPA persist, IDENTITY-generated id).\n11. **Response enrichment** \u2014 builds `OwnerDto` with `bulkSignupWarning` (>80 owners that day) and recomputed membership points/level using real household size.\n12. **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` line with id / customerCode / registrationDate / membershipLevel (the only notification-like effect \u2014 no email/messaging).\n13. **HTTP 201** \u2014 with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and the `OwnerDto` body.\n\n**Notes:** There are no `@InitBinder`, no custom owner `ConstraintValidator`, no `@PrePersist/@PostPersist` or `@EntityListeners`, and no Spring application events on this path. All duplicate/capacity/limit detection is done in-memory in the controller \u2014 there are **no DB uniqueness constraints** on owner telephone/email/identity (the `owners` table has only a PK and NOT-NULL columns)."
